KG42.register("clusters-3e0df05c5dfdafb3343d6fca",{"id":"05-double_auction::v142-d-CL008","paper":"05-double_auction","label":"VCG bilateral rates and conditional operator subsidies","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL008","label":"VCG bilateral rates and conditional operator subsidies","market_meaning":"VCG separately determines the payment rate for the trading buyer and the receipt rate for the seller; when the receipt rate exceeds the payment rate, the operator bears the subsidy needed to cover the shortfall and enable the trade. Unspecified price subscripts leave a gap in numerical closure.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M03"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["pricing","settlement","activation"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"All three chains belong to M03, but the identity of the unsubscripted S^P in the buyer's rate remains unresolved. The subsidy obligation retains its shortfall condition; natural ordering is not used to directly declare that every trade has a strictly positive shortfall.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The bilateral prices directly determine the difference between payments and receipts, and shortfall financing has an explicit source-supported connection to trade execution, so they are combined into a financial and execution candidate; welfare optimality remains separate.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R017","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Retains the separate-component representation of bilateral prices and the original unsubscripted notation."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R018","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Carries the bilateral rate obligations and the conditional operator subsidy."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R016","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Adds the financing requirement for enabling a trade when a shortfall exists."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL008-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R017","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R018","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R017::phi::v141-c-R017-C001","v141-c-R017::phi::v141-c-R017-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R018::phi::v141-c-R018-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-05"],"rationale":"The bilateral buyer and seller prices in Table 1 are implemented as payment and receipt rates, respectively. The separate-component and combined representations are both retained, without treating the buyer's rate and the seller's rate as the same quantity."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL008-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R018","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R016","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R018::phi::v141-c-R018-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R016::phi::v141-c-R016-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-07"],"rationale":"The source text explicitly states that the operator subsidizes the shortfall to enable trade; the settlement obligation and execution requirement are complementary uses under the same condition, and no requires edge is added to the graph."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL008-O01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R017::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R018::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R017::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-05"],"rationale":"Both chains reference the M03 bilateral pricing function; the display representative does not eliminate the difference between buyer and seller rates."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL008-O02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R016::V::settlement.payment","v141-c-R018::V::settlement.payment"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R018::V::settlement.payment","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-07"],"rationale":"When a trade shortfall exists, both chains reference the same M03 settlement and financing function; only the node display is consolidated."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL008-O03","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R017::theta::v141-c-R017-T003","v141-c-R018::theta::v141-c-R018-T05"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-05","v141-b-g01-ev-07"],"rationale":"Within the same VCG auction, both refer to the maximum break-even position on which the price indices depend; this correspondence does not resolve the unsubscripted asking price or the missing index-domain information."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL008-G01","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"S^P in the buyer's rate has no subscript and must not be arbitrarily changed to the marginal asking price. The generic buyer- and seller-price parameters in R017 cover multiple indexed uses and also cannot each be merged as the same quantity with all the differently indexed inputs in R018.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R017","v141-c-R018"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R017::theta::v141-c-R017-T001","v141-c-R017::theta::v141-c-R017-T002","v141-c-R017::phi::v141-c-R017-C001","v141-c-R018::theta::v141-c-R018-T04","v141-c-R018::phi::v141-c-R018-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-05","v141-b-g01-ev-07"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the table subscripts and the definitions and units of the price families and each indexed instance, and have C clarify object granularity; retain the original notation and all parameters in this round."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL008-G02","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The shortfall expression in R018 retains a strict positivity condition, but the unsubscripted asking price prevents closure of its sign determination; equal-price cases also cannot be ruled out by ordering alone. The rate difference is not yet the total monetary subsidy incorporating the traded electricity quantity.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R016","v141-c-R018"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R018::phi::v141-c-R018-C002","v141-c-R016::phi::v141-c-R016-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-05","v141-b-g01-ev-07"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the conditions under which a positive shortfall applies, the equality boundary, and the units; if a monetary-amount rule is needed, obtain the relationship between transaction volume and total subsidy without rewriting the existing strict condition."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL008-G03","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The operator's subsidy responsibility is already represented within the chain, but an independently referenceable object for the shortfall or subsidy amount is missing, and the budget property still lacks an independent ontology representation.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R016","v141-c-R018"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R018::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R018::phi::v141-c-R018-C002","v141-c-R016::E::v141-c-R016-E001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-07"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-prop-03"],"required_work":"Handle the budget-balance proposal manually, and have C determine the subsidy quantity and its graph object; D retains only the existing responsibility interface."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL008-G04","category":"unverified_source","description":"The evidence for VCG rates and subsidies has not been independently reviewed, and the subscript issue in the current B transcription remains unresolved.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R016","v141-c-R017","v141-c-R018"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-05","v141-b-g01-ev-07"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Independently verify Table 1 and the VCG paragraph against the source before checking the mathematics and object declarations."}]},"rule_refs":["05-double_auction::v141-c-R017","05-double_auction::v141-c-R018","05-double_auction::v141-c-R016"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-d8f6aeaeaff5dd0a","COMP-de3c29746c6c77cb","COMP-f4dbfe7382837244","COMP-fc5ef59e0b9fd6df"]});
